{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"esthetical-earthborn-vervet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Enable the approved direct-Anthropic fallback arm in `rebar.toml`\n\nSplit out of [rebar:2876-7958-8dee-4882], where the operator APPROVED direct Anthropic as a\nfallback arm. 2876 fixed the routing defect that made the arm appear broken (the LLM config table\nwas discovered from the ambient cwd rather than the gate's pinned code root, so class-routed\ncalls silently used the built-in bare-Anthropic defaults and 401'd). It deliberately did NOT turn\nthe `fallback` chain on, because doing so was MEASURED to have two blockers that are decisions in\ntheir own right, not bug fixes.\n\n### Blocker 1 — a chain downgrades structured output project-wide (measured)\n\n`runner.py:441` resolves a chain's capabilities as the CONSERVATIVE INTERSECTION across its\ncandidates (`_intersect_capabilities`). `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` is MEASURED\nnative-structured-output-capable ([rebar:18ae], from a Converse PASS) while its direct-Anthropic\ntwin `claude-sonnet-4-6` DELIBERATELY stays PromptedOutput (`capabilities._REBAR_OVERRIDES`,\n\"Do not reintroduce it\"). So adding the arm moves EVERY standard-class call from NativeOutput to\nPromptedOutput — undoing 18ae's measured decision as a side effect of a resilience change.\n\nMEASURED on this ticket: adding `fallback = [{ model = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", provider = \"anthropic\" }]`\nto the `standard` class fails `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py`:\n\n    test_the_native_output_capability_difference_is_measured_and_id_scoped\n    assert (True, True) == (True, False)      # the Bedrock arm started appending the prompted directive\n\nRemoving the chain returns the file to 28 passed / 0 failed. The parity suite is the guard; it\nworks, and it says no.\n\n### Blocker 2 — the credential does not currently work\n\nThe `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` on the development host IS set (108 chars, `sk-ant-` prefix) and is\nREJECTED by Anthropic:\n\n    GET https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models  ->  HTTP 401\n    {\"type\":\"authentication_error\",\"message\":\"API key is invalid.\"}\n\nEnabling an arm whose key 401s buys no redundancy: it converts a legible Bedrock error into a\nmisleading auth error. Note also that `should_fall_back` deliberately excludes credential failures\n(`CHANGE_SETTINGS`), so the chain can never rescue a bad key — the key must simply be valid.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a VALID `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is provisioned for local/CI operation (operator action — this\n      cannot be done from inside a coding session) and verified with the one-line probe in\n      `docs/local-dev-env.md`\n- [ ] the capability-intersection consequence is resolved rather than absorbed: either the\n      direct-Anthropic sonnet id is measured and enabled for native output (repeating 18ae's\n      Converse measurement on the direct arm), or the chain is scoped to the classes where the\n      intersection is provably lossless (frontier/opus is symmetric today), or 18ae's owner\n      explicitly accepts the downgrade with a recorded rationale\n- [ ] `rebar.toml` gains the `fallback` entries and the inline note explaining the blockers is\n      replaced by the decision that cleared them\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` passes UNCHANGED (it must not be relaxed to\n      accommodate the chain — it is the guard that caught this)\n- [ ] a two-sided pin ties the fallback ids to `.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml`, matching\n      how the Bedrock ids are pinned to the bedrock overlay\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py tests/unit/test_project_default_provider.py \\\n           tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py -q","id":"8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Enable the approved direct-Anthropic fallback arm in rebar.toml"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786101830793908001,"uuid":"0488b104-71a9-4176-9dcb-dbbbc3545777"}